# Minception — Cursor Rules

## Project
API Mock Gateway platform. Monorepo with 3 services: mock-service, admin-service, frontend.

## Stack
- Backend: Python 3.11+ / FastAPI / motor (async MongoDB) / Pydantic v2
- Frontend: React 18 / TypeScript 5 / Vite / Tailwind CSS / Shadcn/ui / React Query v5
- Database: MongoDB Atlas (embedded document model — gateways → endpoints → flavors)
- Auth: JWT (PyJWT) + bcrypt, roles: admin / editor / viewer
- Docker + nginx reverse proxy

## Services
- mock-service (port 8001): Stateless request handler. Matches incoming HTTP against MongoDB gateway configs. Read-only.
- admin-service (port 8002): JWT auth, all CRUD, dashboard stats, user management. Calls /reload on mock-service after writes.
- frontend (port 3000): React admin dashboard. Only talks to admin-service.

## API Response Format (ALL endpoints)
```json
{ "success": true, "data": {}, "error": null }
{ "success": false, "data": null, "error": { "code": "ERROR_CODE", "message": "..." } }
```

## Python Rules
- Always use async/await — all FastAPI routes and DB calls must be async
- Use motor (AsyncIOMotorClient) for all MongoDB operations in services
- Use Pydantic v2 with full type hints — no dict returns, always response_model
- Group routes in APIRouter with prefix and tags
- Use Depends() for auth: require_role(["admin", "editor"])
- Raise HTTPException with structured detail: {"code": "...", "message": "..."}
- Never hardcode connection strings — use config.py / env vars

## TypeScript Rules
- Strict mode — no `any` types
- Use React Query for all server state
- JWT interceptor lives in src/services/api.ts — don't duplicate it
- All pages use ProtectedRoute wrapper
- Tailwind classes only — no custom CSS files

## MongoDB Rules
- Embedded document model: gateways.endpoints[].flavors[]
- One read per mock request (no N+1)
- Always include ObjectId for _id
- Timestamps: created_at, updated_at on all top-level documents

## Git
- Branch from develop: feature/name/description
- Never push to main or develop directly
- Commit format: type(scope): description [migration: NNN]

## Key Files
- mock-service/app/engine.py — Core flavor matching logic (most important file)
- migrations/versions/ — All schema migrations (sequential: 001, 002, 003...)
- SCHEMA-VERSIONS.md — Track all schema changes
- docker-compose.local.yml — Run everything locally

## Do NOT
- Add Redis (not in scope)
- Use synchronous pymongo in route handlers (migrations only)
- Modify docker-compose.prod.yml without Wajih's approval
- Skip calling /reload on mock-service after admin writes
- Commit .env files
